# Build context exclusions.
#
# `target/` is the one that matters: it reaches tens of gigabytes, and without
# this every `docker build` would upload all of it to the daemon before reading
# the first line of the Dockerfile.

target/
fuzz/target/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
.git/
.github/

# Artifacts of local runs, never inputs to a build.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
data/
blobs/
*.log

# Documentation and editor state: the image needs none of it — except the
# OpenAPI contract, which `web/src/api/openapi.test.ts` imports and `tsc -b`
# therefore type-checks as part of `npm run build`. It is a build input, not
# documentation, however much its path suggests otherwise.
docs/*
!docs/openapi.json
*.md
!README.md
.vscode/
.idea/
